From 9088f35cb356a8bf4b33d9efc15425bf22649428 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Christian=20K=C3=BCndig?= <christian@kuendig.info>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:23:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] nvapi: Discover CUDA compute GPUs through nvcuda

CudaEnumComputeCapableGpus reported compute GPUs by guessing from the
driver and architecture, so GPUs whose CUDA is provided by other means
were never reported. Ask the public CUDA driver API instead: load
nvcuda.dll, call cuInit, enumerate the devices and match each device's
LUID and node mask against the LUIDs of the adapters DXVK exposes.
Matched adapters are reported in CUDA device order. Adapters reported
by the previous heuristic are kept after them, so nothing changes when
nvcuda.dll is absent, fails to initialize or reports no matching device.

Discovery happens lazily on the first topology query, never during
NvAPI_Initialize, and is cached until the final NvAPI_Unload. Other
entry points never load nvcuda.dll. Concurrent first queries wait for a
single discovery. A CUDA implementation that calls back into NVAPI on
the discovering thread receives the heuristic result instead of
deadlocking.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
